Gears of War 3 (Title Update 6 saves): XamContentCreate's deferred work keeps a copy of the root name, not a
std::string_view into guest memory. With an overlapped call it runs later, when the game has reused the
stack buffer the name was in, so the save device was mounted under garbage ("SG0_0:\PlayerStorage.dat" ->
no device) and the game reported "Error Loading Checkpoints". gow3's CONTENTFIX worked around this for calls
through the XamContentCreateEx thunk only.

diff --git a/src/kernel/xam/xam_content.cpp b/src/kernel/xam/xam_content.cpp
index dd308e7..a8e8ee1 100644
--- a/src/kernel/xam/xam_content.cpp
+++ b/src/kernel/xam/xam_content.cpp
@@ -141,7 +141,9 @@ u32 xeXamContentCreate(u32 user_index, mapped_string root_name, mapped_void cont
     *disposition_ptr = 0;
   }
 
-  auto run = [content_manager, xuid, root_name = root_name.value(), flags, content_data,
+  // A copy: with an overlapped call this runs later, by which time the guest may have reused the
+  // buffer the name was in (a stack buffer in Gears of War 3), and a view would read garbage.
+  auto run = [content_manager, xuid, root_name = std::string(root_name.value()), flags, content_data,
               disposition_ptr,
               license_mask_ptr](uint32_t& extended_error, uint32_t& length) -> X_RESULT {
     X_RESULT result = X_ERROR_INVALID_PARAMETER;
